# netsurf: the browser's functions look like a browser's -- [native code],
# names, WebIDL lengths and attributes; window.close / focus / blur
# (patch 269)
# Generated 2026-10-13
# Base: seleron/vitabrowser (patch stack through 268)
#
# Found tracing hCaptcha's hsw against Chromium (patch 268): it reads the
# property descriptors of 44 window functions and calls toString() on
# them. In this engine 24 of them gave their source text -- the bridge's
# setup scripts and vita_polyfill.js are JavaScript -- where ECMA-262
# requires a built-in function's toString to have the NativeFunction form;
# several were anonymous or named for a helper (matchMedia "",
# getComputedStyle "vgcs", BroadcastChannel "B"), with the helper's
# parameter count as length; operations were sometimes not enumerable and
# interface objects were; window.close / focus / blur were missing outside
# popups. (Chromium given our source-text functions and accessor
# descriptors still passes hCaptcha, so this is not why it refuses us --
# it is a standards fix.)
#
#  - macsurf_qjs.c qjs_eval_builtin: everything qjs_eval_cached compiles is
#    the bridge's own text (setup scripts, the polyfill, event-dispatch
#    snippets -- never a page's), so it is compiled without function
#    source (JS_SetStripFunctionSource, patches/quickjs/02): toString of a
#    built-in gives "function name() { [native code] }". A page's functions
#    keep their source.
#  - vita_polyfill.js, last section: window's own functions get their
#    property's name and Chromium's WebIDL length (a table of the 230
#    non-intrinsic ones both have, tools/hcaptcha/window-ops.js);
#    operations enumerable, interface objects not, interface prototypes
#    their @@toStringTag (when the prototype is the constructor's own);
#    scroll is no longer scrollTo itself; webkitURL / WebKitCSSMatrix stay
#    aliases; close() closes a window a script opened and otherwise does
#    nothing (as in browsers), focus() / blur() do nothing; the engine's
#    helpers (__vita*, _k, ...) no longer enumerate. Left: DOMMatrixReadOnly
#    / DOMPointReadOnly are DOMMatrix / DOMPoint themselves; window.stop()
#    does not exist (nothing here can stop a load from script).
#
# Gate: testpages/pages/JS-builtins-native.html (BUILTIN 8/8, Chromium
# 8/8).
